 "verdict_reason": "Downgraded at integration (2026-09-25): replication is technical only (same transduction), a WT-vs-WT null reproduces ~32% of the hit rate at z<=-4, and there is no independent same-line or cross-study check. Original agent reason: Borderline include. Technical split-half AUROC 0.96/0.91 (>=0.84 for every query), hit rate 0.23% (245 pos; 0.11-0.43% per query, no hub), fitness-only AUROC 0.67, recovers CDK12-CDK13 and ARID1A-ARID1B. Caveats: replicates are technical only (no second clone); a parental-vs-parental null implies ~30% FDR at the chosen cut-off; no same-line cross-study overlap, and the different-line overlap with feng2022 (STK11, ARID1A in HEK293-A) is at chance (0.46 with 98 of our positives; 0.51 for their 27) - not counted as a contradiction because lines differ and feng2022 itself fails its null calibration. If SLB requires independent (biological/cross-study) replication, downgrade to measurements-only.",
 "verdict_agent": "include"
}